<title>GERMANY: Hoechst details 96 profit.</title>
<headline>Hoechst details 96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   2,774   vs 2,245</p>
<p>    Group sales				  50,927  vs 52,177</p>
<p>     group foreign sales		     41,758  vs 41,135</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     5,280   vs 4,091</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		   4,013   vs 3,591</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share(DVFA)	 2.75    vs 2.40 marks</p>
<p>    Group return on equity after tax     16.5    vs 15.3 pct</p>
<p>    Group return on total assets	   11.7    vs 10.7 pct</p>
<p>    Group fixed assets and investments   31,710  vs 29,520</p>
<p>    Group research costs		     3,880   vs 3,479</p>
<p>    Group personnel expenses		 13,848  vs 14,345</p>
<p>(Excluding restructuring charges)</p>
<p>    Group workforce (annual average)     151,486 vs 165,928</p>
<p>    Group cash flow			    5,622   vs 5,792</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax income from divestment 2,523   vs 1,111</p>
<p>    Group restructuring costs		682     vs 1,016</p>
<p>    Group corporate debt		     11,819  vs 12,730</p>
<p>    Group interest expense		   1,082   vs 942</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  958     vs 1,504</p>
<p>    Parent pre-tax profit		    1,898   vs 2,359</p>
<p>    Parent sales				 12,422  vs 14,190</p>
<p>    Dividend (already reported)	    1.40    vs 1.30 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of German chemicals and pharmaceuticals company is Hoechst AG. Analysts had predicted that sales would fall an average three percent percent to come in between 50.2 billion and 51.183 billion marks. Pre-tax profit however was expected to surge 50 percent to between 6.0 billion and 6.375 billion marks. Analysts had said the huge swing in profits would be largely attributable to Hoechst's divestments in 1996. Some of the numbers were already reported on Tuesday after the group announced its dividend.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
